---
description: Security rules for git access and packaging
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security

- Never commit credentials, tokens, private keys, or secret env files.
- Invoke git only via argv lists — never `shell=True`.
- Validate repository paths with `Path.resolve()` and reject traversal.
- Resolve branch and ref names through `for-each-ref` before use.
- Disable hooks for inspected repositories (`core.hooksPath=/dev/null`).
- Apply timeouts and result size limits to every git invocation.
- Do not expose full patches by default — commit messages and metadata only.
- Candidate clone-from-URL work must validate schemes, reject `ext::` and custom upload-pack, enforce size and timeout limits, and isolate clones on disk.
